Introduction {#s1}
============

Cyclotides are proteins of \~30 amino acid residues that are characterized by the cyclic cystine knot (CCK) motif (Craik et al., [@B11]; Burman et al., [@B5]). The CCK motif consists of six conserved cysteines that form three disulfide bonds and a head to tail cyclic backbone (Figure [1A](#F1){ref-type="fig"}). The cyclotides have been classified into two main subfamilies, the Möbius and the bracelets,
